guous B. This avoids non-contiguity and shape mismatch with self.weight. We adopt this approach.",
    "evidence": [
      "Log shows failure at model_new.py line 30: x = cuda_extension.addmm_forward(self.bias, x, self.weight) after previous rollback, causing 'mat2 rows must equal K'.",
      "The reference code uses `torch.addmm(self.bias, x, self.weight.t())`, with weight.t() shape [input_size, hidden_size]. Passing self.weight directly (shape [hidden_size, input_size]) is semantically equivalent if kernel computes A*B^T.",
      "The current binding likely validates mat2.size(0) == K (input_size) causing failure when passing self.weight. Repair context shows rejected attempts with similar shape mismatch errors.",
      "The custom kernel in custom_ops.cu currently computes sum += A[row*K+k] * B[col*K+k], assuming B is [N,K]. If we pass self.weight (which is [N,K]), this computation is exactly A*weight^T, matching reference.",
